==Lithuanian==

===Etymology===
A modern coinage, with components derived from {{cog|grc|βίος||life}} and {{m|grc|-λογία||branch of study}}, with variants that arose in various European languages around 1800. It was borrowed into Lithuanian and adapted (e.g. {{suffix|lt||-ija}}).

